ority: P1\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 5\n\n- plan_id: plan_007\n  claim: [Claim 3]\n  name: \"Diversity-capability tradeoff visualization\"\n  description: >\n    Plot K_eff vs η_max across all C(n,3) panels for n=15+ models. Fit tradeoff curve.\n    Show Pareto frontier. Stratify by capability tier.\n  priority: P2\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 2\n\n- plan_id: plan_008\n  claim: [Claim 1, Claim 6]\n  name: \"Panel size sensitivity: K=3,5,7,9\"\n  description: >\n    Test weakest-link theorem for different panel sizes. Does η_max dominance\n    persist as K grows? At what K does diversity start mattering (if ever)?\n    Critical for practical panel design recommendations.\n  priority: P2\n  depends_on: [plan_001]\n  estimated_gpu_hours: 30\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013yYuADteP47CBBkQRwg2KP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the experiment plan. Let me also check the registry and any other relevant files for context on completed experiments.\n\nLet me now generate the detailed median-tier predictions for each planned experiment (plan_001 through plan_008).\n\nFor the median tier:\n- η_max significant in 60-75% conditions\n- K_eff ~70% non-significant in adaptive, but ~15% weakly significant negative (diversity helps slightly)\n- API models introduce new regime where weakest-link weakens\n- BFT contrast direction correct but Cohen's d moderate\n- Two-stage algorithm wins 60-80% but no significant difference in all-strong regime\n\n\n- The narrative is shifting from \"diversity never helps\" to \"individual robustness is dominant, with diversity playing only a marginal role when robustness is already high\"\n\nNow I'm mapping each experiment to its expected median-tier results. For plan_001 with scale expansion across 15+ models including API variants, I expect to see some weakening of the weakest-link effect due to all-strong model panels, η_max remaining significant in most but not all conditions, K_eff emerging as weakly significant in certain all-strong-model panels, and a diversity-capability tradeoff correlation around -0.6 overall, dropping to -0.3 within tiers. For plan_002 with attack expansion across 6+ attack types...\n\nContinuing with attack analysis...\n\nThe per-judge concentration shows high Gini coefficients but the weakest link effect isn't as pronounced as in the optimistic tier. Looking at the diversity-capability tradeoff, there's a strong negative correlation around -0.65 overall, though it weakens to about -0.3 when examining within individual tiers. Panel size sensitivity reveals that η_max maintains dominance at smaller panel sizes, but this advantage erodes as we scale to larger panels—at K=9, K_eff finally shows some marginal significance. Now I'm preparing the full YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7515,"cache_read_input_tokens":21082,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7515},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"790d1674-f3e2-44e8-8259-048eca3893b4","uuid":"f653e72e-3568-41d6-bbe6-f7303d818caf"}
